  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CareDisc 5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "As a caregiver for a loved one with cancer, you decide to attend a community
    meeting hosted by a cancer research foundation. When asked what types of new
    treatments families hope to see, you share that your partner\u2019s current treatment
    options have caused extreme fatigue and nausea, emphasizing your hope for new
    treatments with fewer side effects so patients can enjoy daily life more.\n\nHow
    could this feedback help researchers during the Discovery stage?"
  explanation: "While caregivers may not be directly involved in research studies,
    their voices can still shape what scientists focus on in early research. By sharing
    what patients go through \u2014 like fatigue, pain, or emotional challenges \u2014
    they help researchers understand what kinds of treatments could make the biggest
    difference. Their input reminds researchers that it\u2019s not just about finding
    new ways to fight cancer, but about helping patients live better and feel better,
    too."
  correctAnswer: 'A: It could inspire them to focus on new treatments that target
    cancer cells more precisely and are gentler on the body.'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'B: It could change how doctors prescribe existing treatment
    options to patients.'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'C: It could help them decide which patients and how many will
    be selected for a clinical trial.'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'D: It could help new treatments get approved and become available
    to all patients faster.'
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
